f the paper  so just take it and fold it down to the  other end  just like that  and then you can make another crease  along the top  so you should have a piece of paper that  looks just like this  now we're going to take one end of the  paper and fold it across to the other  end of the paper  just like that  and you might want to do this on a flat  surface i like to hold it up to the  camera so you guys can see what i'm  doing so once you align it edge to edge  then you can kind of tug on it here  to round that off  and make a crease on the end here  okay so once you fold it like that then  we're going to open it  and then you just want to hold it  so that you have the piece of paper  vertically positioned just like that now  i'm just going to draw a horizontal line  on that fold which we just made  just so it's a little easier for you to  see  and then we're going to take the paper  and we're going to take the bottom half  of it  and we want to fold it to the left onto  that line so that this edge on the right  on the bottom right here lines up with  that that line i drew  so you want to fold it just like that to  the left and make a crease along the  bottom here  then we're going to take the bottom of  the paper and fold it straight up along  that line  and it's probably easier to do these  folds on a flat surface  and you want to make sure everything  stays nice and flat  after you make these new folds  so just make some creases along the  paper  and then you'll see we have some excess  paper here on the left and what you want  to do with this paper is you want to  fold it behind the model  on this line here that we have so you  want to fold it back all the way until  it comes around the other side  and then you want to make a crease on  the left side of the model  now what you're going to do with this  little excess paper is you're going to  fold it  where it meets this edge here so you  want to fold it to the left just like  that  and make a crease  then you can take the excess paper and  as you'll see we have a little bit of a  triangular pocket here  and you could just tuck this excess  paper right into that pocket  and just make sure everything is nice  and flat now we want to take the top of  the paper and we want to fold it  straight down along this line here where  the paper meets the top of this edge so  let me just draw a line  so that you can see where i'm talking  about  just fold the paper straight down along  that line so you want to take it  and fold it straight down  and then just make a crease along the  top of the paper  now if you hold the model if you flip it  around you'll see there's excess paper  that overhangs the model here what you  want to do is you just want to fold up  along this edge here now  so the paper kind of wraps around and  then just make a crease along the bottom  okay so now you can just open everything  back up  and then what we're going to do  you'll see this is the little the tip of  the paper which we kind of wrapped  around  the bottom of this we want to just fold  straight downwards on that fold now and  then just make another good crease  and remember this pocket here that we  had previously the triangular pocket  we're going to take the whole half  the top half of the model now and we're  going to tuck it into that triangular  pocket so you want to just open it  and you want to tuck the model  you want to tuck the rest of the paper  into that pocket  and then you want to make a really good  crease  along the outside of the paper here  so you should have a model that looks  just like this  then what we're going to do is we're  going to take this corner  and you want to fold it to the other  corner  straight along this edge here  so you want to just take the whole model  and just fold it in half  along that edge the paper gets a little  thick here but  the loose leaf paper definitely makes it  a lot easier to make this fold  you just want to fold it in half like  that  and make